WEBVTT

00:02.360 --> 00:04.329
I will...

00:04.330 --> 00:06.860
make your wish come true.

00:13.680 --> 00:17.410
Because I can sense that
your wish and my wish...

00:20.080 --> 00:23.850
are the same.

00:36.770 --> 00:39.230
But then...

00:42.540 --> 00:44.560
why are you crying?

00:57.150 --> 00:59.089
Ow, my head...

00:59.090 --> 01:02.959
Tea and pickled plums
work best for hangovers.

01:02.960 --> 01:04.120
Here.

01:05.260 --> 01:06.759
Thank you, Grandma...

01:06.760 --> 01:08.559
What a sad drunk.

01:08.560 --> 01:10.269
Shut up...

01:10.270 --> 01:13.329
Oh my. Ru-<i>chan</i>, look at the time.

01:13.330 --> 01:15.570
Yup, I know.

01:18.310 --> 01:19.339
Time...?

01:19.340 --> 01:22.470
She's going out with her friend.

01:24.280 --> 01:25.650
Sour...!

01:30.590 --> 01:31.990
Nice!

01:41.600 --> 01:43.929
Have fun, you hear?

01:43.930 --> 01:46.269
Okay.

01:46.270 --> 01:47.699
What is it, Bro?

01:47.700 --> 01:51.369
All right. Let your kind, big
brother here send you out.

01:51.370 --> 01:52.709
What? No way!

01:52.710 --> 01:54.379
I'm going!

01:54.380 --> 01:57.379
See you later.

01:57.380 --> 01:59.110
She refused me...

02:16.500 --> 02:19.470
If a pillar goes there...

02:46.690 --> 02:48.199
<i>Taken and granted,</i>

02:48.200 --> 02:52.199
<i>ideals are repetitious
games that slip through</i>

02:52.200 --> 02:54.899
<i>My daily life is so shot with holes</i>

02:54.900 --> 02:57.769
<i>that I can barely stand</i>

02:57.770 --> 02:59.069
<i>Empty theories without conclusions</i>

02:59.070 --> 03:03.339
<i>Dance steps along invisible rules</i>

03:03.340 --> 03:08.379
<i>The final bell holding
together the crumbling day rings</i>

03:08.380 --> 03:12.789
<i>In the scene I imagine</i>

03:12.790 --> 03:15.459
<i>you're there</i>

03:15.460 --> 03:18.259
<i>with a smile</i>

03:18.260 --> 03:23.769
<i>No forgiveness? No desires?</i>

03:23.770 --> 03:27.200
<i>And still</i>

03:28.800 --> 03:32.039
<i>We cry "OPEN"</i>

03:32.040 --> 03:36.309
<i>A future to get back and a world to destroy</i>

03:36.310 --> 03:38.779
<i>A wish to open. GOT IT?</i>

03:38.780 --> 03:40.449
<i>Now cross</i>

03:40.450 --> 03:43.119
<i>I wish you don't cry</i>

03:43.120 --> 03:50.119
<i>The future of light and dark,
let's believe in the "future"</i>

03:50.120 --> 03:56.620
<i>so that they overlap to gain color again</i>

04:04.740 --> 04:07.179
There are a lot of couples...

04:07.180 --> 04:08.939
I don't think we really fit here.

04:08.940 --> 04:10.649
What are you saying?

04:10.650 --> 04:13.649
There could be a wonderful
encounter, you know?

04:13.650 --> 04:15.249
Someone might pick you up!

04:15.250 --> 04:16.180
P-Pick up?!

04:16.181 --> 04:18.519
Huh?! That's not good!

04:18.520 --> 04:19.949
C'mon, why not?

04:19.950 --> 04:22.089
Y-Yuzuki, were you asked out before?!
Wha-?!

04:22.090 --> 04:23.689
Um, ah, yes...

04:23.690 --> 04:27.329
Really?! How was he?
How did he ask you out?

04:27.330 --> 04:30.299
Um... Oh, come on, let's just go!

04:30.300 --> 04:32.699
So, did you go out someplace with him?

04:32.700 --> 04:35.769
It's really not worth talking about...

04:35.770 --> 04:37.469
Aww... No fair.

04:37.470 --> 04:40.870
Tell me! I want to know! I want to know!

04:49.150 --> 04:50.450
Over there!

05:08.070 --> 05:11.300
"Girl meets Girl Festival"

05:13.070 --> 05:14.890
"Lunch bag" "Warmer cover"

05:14.580 --> 05:17.209
Wow, so cute!

05:14.891 --> 05:16.710
"Handkerchief" "Accessory pouch" "Welcome"

05:17.210 --> 05:18.995
I think I can afford this.

05:18.996 --> 05:20.480
"Coaster"

05:20.481 --> 05:23.249
Yup. This is more like us.

05:23.250 --> 05:26.850
Maybe I'll get this for Grandma.

05:27.920 --> 05:31.329
I'm so glad to see Ruko having fun...

05:31.330 --> 05:32.520
Yeah.

05:44.870 --> 05:48.509
I'm going to buy you a
matching pair of scrunchies, too.

05:48.510 --> 05:50.210
Ru!

05:54.580 --> 05:56.349
Ruko!

05:56.350 --> 05:58.619
Look. Isn't it cute?

05:58.620 --> 06:01.210
You're right! Can I get a closer look?

06:07.700 --> 06:10.629
It's quiet over here.

06:10.630 --> 06:13.029
Why don't we take a short break?

06:13.030 --> 06:15.139
Okay.

06:15.140 --> 06:16.470
Ruko!

06:19.310 --> 06:20.779
Hitoe?

06:20.780 --> 06:24.149
I'm sorry. My friends in
Aomori asked me to take a pic.

06:24.150 --> 06:25.080
Your friends?

06:25.081 --> 06:26.409
Yup!

06:26.410 --> 06:32.549
I wrote to them that I made friends in Tokyo,
and they sent me an e-mail asking for more.

06:32.550 --> 06:33.580
Here.

06:35.390 --> 06:38.589
Show me, too!

06:38.590 --> 06:41.059
I kept...

06:41.060 --> 06:44.269
wishing for friends, but...

06:44.270 --> 06:47.569
I guess I had friends all along.

06:47.570 --> 06:48.800
Yup.

06:52.440 --> 06:54.679
Maybe I should get a mobile, too.

06:54.680 --> 06:55.480
Huh?

06:55.481 --> 06:57.679
That came out of nowhere.

06:57.680 --> 07:01.249
If I have a mobile, then I can
get in touch with friends quickly.

07:01.250 --> 07:04.619
It helps if something
happens, or if I'm far away...

07:04.620 --> 07:06.789
Say, can I take a look?
Yup!

07:06.790 --> 07:09.619
Well, how about we go
shopping for mobiles next time?

07:09.620 --> 07:10.689
Sounds good!

07:10.690 --> 07:14.429
But are you sure you'll
be able to use one, Ruko?

07:14.430 --> 07:16.299
Huh? Is it that hard to use?

07:16.300 --> 07:17.599
Don't worry.

07:17.600 --> 07:19.869
Hm... I guess we'll go to Akihabara then.

07:19.870 --> 07:21.999
Huh?
No matter what happens...

07:22.000 --> 07:23.639
Even if I go far away...

07:23.640 --> 07:25.339
Don't you know?

07:25.340 --> 07:28.509
You can only buy mobiles in Akihabara!

07:28.510 --> 07:31.309
Not true! They were being
sold near my place too.

07:31.310 --> 07:33.309
Sure, only the mobile itself.

07:33.310 --> 07:35.819
You can't sign-up except in Akihabara!

07:35.820 --> 07:37.149
Huh?! Seriously?!

07:37.150 --> 07:39.189
I don't want to lose anyone anymore.

07:39.190 --> 07:40.889
Oh, Yuzuki...

07:40.890 --> 07:42.859
She's lying. You can buy them anywhere.

07:42.860 --> 07:46.659
Really? You surprised me there.

07:46.660 --> 07:49.229
You better discuss it
with your grandma, too.

07:49.230 --> 07:51.829
Anyone.

07:51.830 --> 07:55.139
I'm getting thirsty. How about
we get something to drink?

07:55.140 --> 07:56.140
Okay!

07:57.140 --> 07:58.169
So...

07:58.170 --> 08:00.169
why ice cream?

08:00.170 --> 08:01.709
It looks tasty!

08:01.710 --> 08:05.049
Hold on! There's no one
around! You know why?!

08:05.050 --> 08:06.349
It's cold!

08:06.350 --> 08:08.080
It's winter!

08:27.440 --> 08:30.269
I'll have caramel flavor.

08:30.270 --> 08:31.710
Ruko?

08:41.050 --> 08:44.189
What's the matter?

08:44.190 --> 08:45.710
Nothing...

08:47.520 --> 08:49.389
Hitoe? Let's get out of here...

08:49.390 --> 08:51.050
Ruko...

08:53.900 --> 08:55.890
"Group A"

08:58.730 --> 09:00.469
WIXOSS...

09:00.470 --> 09:01.200
Open!

09:01.201 --> 09:04.909
What gives, having a
competition at a place like this?

09:04.910 --> 09:07.579
Are there any... Selectors?

09:07.580 --> 09:10.070
No... Let's go.

09:17.750 --> 09:19.589
Ah, hey, wait a second!

09:19.590 --> 09:20.919
Yuzuki?

09:20.920 --> 09:22.919
There's... one here...

09:22.920 --> 09:24.089
Here...?

09:24.090 --> 09:25.429
A Selector?!

09:25.430 --> 09:26.889
She's coming...

09:26.890 --> 09:29.129
Closer... She's coming closer...!

09:29.130 --> 09:30.499
I found you!

09:30.500 --> 09:32.929
Selector...!

09:32.930 --> 09:35.560
Can you battle me, please?!

09:37.270 --> 09:38.760
She's...!

09:40.810 --> 09:43.239
She's... a Selector?

09:43.240 --> 09:46.849
I'm sorry there for my girl's loud voice.

09:46.850 --> 09:49.619
See, look Eldora!
It's exactly like Chiyori said!

09:49.620 --> 09:51.649
I told you we could find Selectors here!

09:51.650 --> 09:54.459
And two of them! Could this be fate?!

09:54.460 --> 09:58.459
Duh, they're having a competition.
Of course you'd find some.

09:58.460 --> 10:01.829
I guess us heroines can't
avoid the fate of battle...

10:01.830 --> 10:05.799
What?! Avoid? You're looking for battle!

10:05.800 --> 10:08.139
Pooh! Eldora, go with the flow!

10:08.140 --> 10:11.339
I'm so sorry! She's like this all the time.

10:11.340 --> 10:14.109
So, anyways...

10:14.110 --> 10:15.110
Yay!

10:15.111 --> 10:18.709
Please battle Chiyori!

10:18.710 --> 10:20.180
Battle...

10:32.530 --> 10:34.399
The back alley!

10:34.400 --> 10:37.300
Mmm...! So battle-ly!

10:38.900 --> 10:44.839
Speaking of, did you folks
go to Urazoe Iona's fan event?

10:44.840 --> 10:47.509
You went, right?

10:47.510 --> 10:50.179
You know, we just couldn't make it there.

10:50.180 --> 10:52.010
E-Eldora!

10:55.320 --> 10:56.810
<i>Open</i>!

10:58.920 --> 11:01.319
Huh...? What...?

11:01.320 --> 11:03.359
My kid here is lousy with directions.

11:03.360 --> 11:04.859
It took a couple hours,

11:04.860 --> 11:09.199
circling around the area over and over again, just
to find the location earlier. The other day...

11:09.200 --> 11:10.000
Wha-?!

11:10.001 --> 11:12.399
Eldora... zip your mouth! Zip it!

11:12.400 --> 11:15.369
G-G-Give! I give! I give!

11:15.370 --> 11:16.699
So, anyways...

11:16.700 --> 11:22.209
The beautiful maidens' battle
for their wishes is about to begin!

11:22.210 --> 11:23.870
<i>Open</i>!

11:26.080 --> 11:28.549
Huh? What? Huh?

11:28.550 --> 11:30.179
We... won't battle.

11:30.180 --> 11:31.090
Huh?

11:31.091 --> 11:34.459
We're not going to battle.

11:34.460 --> 11:35.390
Oh my.

11:35.391 --> 11:37.019
But, you're Selectors.

11:37.020 --> 11:40.229
Your wish won't come true!

11:40.230 --> 11:43.599
I guess you don't know what
happens if you lose your battles.

11:43.600 --> 11:45.399
Huh?

11:45.400 --> 11:47.739
What...! Are...! You saying?!

11:47.740 --> 11:49.539
I knowey.

11:49.540 --> 11:51.569
Death awaits those who lose seven times...

11:51.570 --> 11:53.769
The WIXOSS factors
spread inside your body...

11:53.770 --> 11:56.439
then from the inside you
go <i>kaboom</i>! <i>Squish</i>! <i>Splat</i>!

11:56.440 --> 11:58.749
No...!

11:58.750 --> 12:04.780
If you lose three times, you
lose your rights and wish, then...

12:06.450 --> 12:09.559
that very wish is reversed.

12:09.560 --> 12:13.159
If your wish was to be wealthy...

12:13.160 --> 12:17.969
Losing in battle means that you lose
all wealth, and plummeted to poverty.

12:17.970 --> 12:21.399
If your wish was to become
skilled in playing the piano...

12:21.400 --> 12:24.569
You may lose your piano, or you may
become incapable of playing the piano...

12:24.570 --> 12:28.109
In any case, you won't be
able to play the piano, forever...

12:28.110 --> 12:32.149
Hitoe's wish was "to make friends"...

12:32.150 --> 12:35.080
With that wish reversed...

12:38.690 --> 12:42.019
Wish reversed? That's...

12:42.020 --> 12:43.259
a new setting?!

12:43.260 --> 12:44.789
Ouch...

12:44.790 --> 12:48.459
My wish came true
without relying on WIXOSS.

12:48.460 --> 12:49.460
So you should...

12:49.461 --> 12:53.299
But, but, getting your happiness
through battling is better...

12:53.300 --> 12:55.869
Winning in battle...
Hm?

12:55.870 --> 12:59.609
Winning in battle isn't
going to make you happy!

12:59.610 --> 13:02.479
Winning battles aren't enough.

13:02.480 --> 13:07.879
You can't become an Eternal Girl
without your LRIG accepting your wish.

13:07.880 --> 13:09.820
Are you sure about this?

13:15.860 --> 13:18.189
I accept...

13:18.190 --> 13:20.899
I... accept!

13:20.900 --> 13:25.229
the laws of the Selector.

13:25.230 --> 13:26.329
And...!

13:26.330 --> 13:30.539
now, a new Eternal Girl will be born!

13:30.540 --> 13:32.240
- "The Flames of Void Play
- the Victory Song of Oblivion"

13:30.570 --> 13:32.339
Yessy, I know!

13:32.340 --> 13:35.739
"How an LRIG is Born"! The
second volume to the WIXOSS novel!

13:35.740 --> 13:39.879
WIXOSS 2! <i>The Flames of Void</i>
<i>Play the Victory Song of Oblivion</i>!

13:39.880 --> 13:42.179
And that's how you get
your wish to come truey!

13:42.180 --> 13:43.419
That's not it.

13:43.420 --> 13:47.019
Hitoe... Show me to her.

13:47.020 --> 13:47.990
What?

13:47.991 --> 13:49.889
Say, Chiyori?
Huh?

13:49.890 --> 13:52.729
Do you... remember me?

13:52.730 --> 13:54.060
Huh?

13:56.260 --> 13:57.100
Hmm...

13:57.101 --> 13:58.699
Ah! I knew it!

13:58.700 --> 14:01.869
I thought I sensed something I felt before.

14:01.870 --> 14:05.109
Chiyori, Chiyori! It's her, you know? Her!

14:05.110 --> 14:05.870
What?

14:05.871 --> 14:11.079
She's the one who beat you in
your very first battle you offered!

14:11.080 --> 14:12.849
Whaaaa?!

14:12.850 --> 14:15.619
What?! Why are you a card?!

14:15.620 --> 14:18.919
My wish came true, and I replaced my LRIG.

14:18.920 --> 14:22.089
Oh, really? You too?

14:22.090 --> 14:24.859
Look carefully... This is what happens!

14:24.860 --> 14:29.629
I can't go to school or
eat ice cream any more.

14:29.630 --> 14:32.229
Even the person I love...

14:32.230 --> 14:36.739
Tama can't make Ruko into an LRIG...

14:36.740 --> 14:39.230
I don't want to say bye to Ruko...

14:40.910 --> 14:44.409
Even if you win the battles,
you're going to become just like me!

14:44.410 --> 14:45.749
Eldora, was it?

14:45.750 --> 14:48.449
Eh? Ah, yes, what is it?

14:48.450 --> 14:53.949
If you're an LRIG, then you must know about
that white windowed room, and that girl, Mayu!

14:53.950 --> 14:56.619
Are you letting her battle
knowing what happens?!

14:56.620 --> 14:59.989
Well, my memories have
been fleeting recently and...

14:59.990 --> 15:03.099
I have no idea what
you're talking about.

15:03.100 --> 15:04.999
It seems she understands now.

15:05.000 --> 15:06.000
Yup.

15:06.001 --> 15:09.099
So, you shouldn't battle...

15:09.100 --> 15:10.969
<i>Yaaaaaah</i>!

15:10.970 --> 15:13.009
It's exactly the same as the novel!

15:13.010 --> 15:17.339
The heroine becomes a card,
and the story is to be continued!

15:17.340 --> 15:22.749
Going into the world of WIXOSS
is like, Chiyori's dream come true!

15:22.750 --> 15:25.119
So happy!
Wha...?!

15:25.120 --> 15:27.449
<i>Chiyo-rinda</i>!

15:27.450 --> 15:28.589
Chiyo-ringa...

15:28.590 --> 15:30.929
Chiyo-rumba, Chori-Chori...

15:30.930 --> 15:34.999
Which do you think is better for
my name when I become an LRIG?

15:35.000 --> 15:37.159
I don't think you need one...

15:37.160 --> 15:41.339
What? Eldora, I bet you think
Chiyori can't get her wish to come true!

15:41.340 --> 15:45.639
No-I-believe-in-you-from-the-bottom-of-my-heart.

15:45.640 --> 15:47.509
Why the monotone read?!

15:47.510 --> 15:49.939
What should we do?

15:49.940 --> 15:52.009
Ru...

15:52.010 --> 15:54.210
Say, Ru...?

15:56.120 --> 15:58.489
Stop...

15:58.490 --> 15:59.519
Stop!

15:59.520 --> 16:01.219
Ruko?!

16:01.220 --> 16:03.120
Wait, Ruko!

16:04.660 --> 16:06.220
Huh?

16:14.070 --> 16:17.039
Wait...! Ruko!

16:17.040 --> 16:20.209
Ru... Tama will battle.

16:20.210 --> 16:23.179
This will be the last battle.

16:23.180 --> 16:25.200
White Hope!

16:30.350 --> 16:31.519
No...

16:31.520 --> 16:33.920
Ruko won, so why...?!

16:35.590 --> 16:37.150
Ruko...

16:39.530 --> 16:41.020
Hitoe?

16:45.200 --> 16:46.930
It's going away!

16:48.600 --> 16:49.869
Wait...

16:49.870 --> 16:51.739
No...

16:51.740 --> 16:53.669
Don't... Please don't...

16:53.670 --> 16:57.039
Now, a new Eternal Girl...

16:57.040 --> 16:58.749
will be born!

16:58.750 --> 17:01.180
Don't...!

17:15.730 --> 17:19.560
What's with the long face, Ru?

17:21.440 --> 17:23.730
My Selector...

17:25.210 --> 17:27.570
Iona-<i>san...</i>

17:29.740 --> 17:30.740
Tama...

17:30.741 --> 17:32.110
Why...?!

17:38.720 --> 17:40.089
Tama...

17:40.090 --> 17:42.419
Where are you, Tama?!

17:42.420 --> 17:44.550
Tama...!

17:48.100 --> 17:50.059
Iona-<i>san...</i>

17:50.060 --> 17:51.599
What's going on?

17:51.600 --> 17:55.069
Weren't you listening to
what Urith was saying?

17:55.070 --> 17:58.609
Iona-<i>san</i> won more than enough battles.

17:58.610 --> 18:02.909
But, you lacked a condition
to get your wish to come true.

18:02.910 --> 18:06.309
So the condition was met,
and your wish came true?

18:06.310 --> 18:08.910
Iona-<i>san</i>, what is your wish?

18:10.320 --> 18:12.620
To be an LRIG.

18:13.950 --> 18:17.619
To become an LRIG to someone stronger
than me, so as to continue battles.

18:17.620 --> 18:20.989
So the last condition
was to lose in battle?!

18:20.990 --> 18:24.669
Your wish came true
because you lost to Ruko?!

18:24.670 --> 18:26.699
But, how...?

18:26.700 --> 18:29.639
That doesn't matter now.

18:29.640 --> 18:32.169
It was great.

18:32.170 --> 18:35.539
I'm so glad... Ru...

18:35.540 --> 18:37.209
Tama...

18:37.210 --> 18:40.279
Where did Tama go...?

18:40.280 --> 18:42.150
Who knows?

18:43.720 --> 18:44.989
Tama...

18:44.990 --> 18:47.010
Tama...!

18:52.490 --> 18:55.159
You should have... battled her.

18:55.160 --> 18:56.999
I'm not going to battle!

18:57.000 --> 18:58.899
You want to meet Tama, right?

18:58.900 --> 19:02.239
That wish may come true... If you battle...

19:02.240 --> 19:04.869
No. I...

19:04.870 --> 19:06.309
I won't...

19:06.310 --> 19:09.479
Then why do you still have me?

19:09.480 --> 19:12.740
If you're not going to battle,
you should throw me away.

19:14.180 --> 19:17.210
I knew it. You want to do it...

19:20.520 --> 19:22.510
Such attachment...

19:30.200 --> 19:32.429
Ruko...

19:32.430 --> 19:34.999
I wasn't going to ask, but...

19:35.000 --> 19:37.599
Why did you bring her with you?

19:37.600 --> 19:39.409
Don't tell me you wanted to battle...

19:39.410 --> 19:42.709
If you battled again, there's
no telling what would happen.

19:42.710 --> 19:45.709
She's right! Tama disappearing...

19:45.710 --> 19:49.679
Iona becoming Ruko's card...
No one could have expected it!

19:49.680 --> 19:53.549
Something worse may happen next!
But...!

19:53.550 --> 19:55.919
But, I want to meet Tama...

19:55.920 --> 20:01.229
I still... I want to help
Yuzuki, and everyone else...

20:01.230 --> 20:02.899
Even so...

20:02.900 --> 20:04.129
You shouldn't battle!

20:04.130 --> 20:07.069
I know... I know, but...!

20:07.070 --> 20:09.560
What should I...!

20:10.740 --> 20:15.879
I don't know what to do
either, so let's all think together.

20:15.880 --> 20:18.749
Right. You're not alone, Ruko.

20:18.750 --> 20:20.549
We're with you.

20:20.550 --> 20:23.879
Let's all get through this, together!

20:23.880 --> 20:25.389
Hitoe...

20:25.390 --> 20:27.050
Yuzuki...

20:29.760 --> 20:32.559
There are too many
things I don't understand.

20:32.560 --> 20:35.999
Why isn't Ruko battling?

20:36.000 --> 20:40.330
Like me, she seeks battles...

20:41.440 --> 20:43.439
And her wish...

20:43.440 --> 20:46.939
I want to help Yuzuki, and everyone else...

20:46.940 --> 20:51.949
An LRIG only accepts a wish
they believe they can make true.

20:51.950 --> 20:56.749
Despite abandoning the
wish, why did she believe...

20:56.750 --> 21:00.249
she could make such an
impossible wish come true?

21:00.250 --> 21:03.590
Ruko's LRIG... is me.

21:04.630 --> 21:07.490
I'll change Ruko...

21:09.000 --> 21:12.330
Instead of clinging on
to an impossible wish...

21:13.970 --> 21:17.369
I want her to sense the excitement...

21:17.370 --> 21:19.970
To battle to her heart's desire...

21:26.380 --> 21:28.110
Along with me...

21:31.390 --> 21:34.450
Next is Shinjuku. Shinjuku.

21:38.490 --> 21:42.829
She's my clue... to find Tama.

21:42.830 --> 21:44.869
Did you say something?

21:44.870 --> 21:47.299
No...

21:47.300 --> 21:49.170
Nothing at all...

21:52.540 --> 21:55.970
"This Silent Beginning"

21:53.510 --> 21:55.180
Nothing...

22:02.480 --> 22:04.049
<i>Life...</i>

22:04.050 --> 22:09.489
<i>A city of mazes with no exit</i>

22:09.490 --> 22:14.059
<i>and the sound of bells ringing</i>

22:14.060 --> 22:15.659
<i>I do...</i>

22:15.660 --> 22:21.269
<i>Leave the "now" handed to me</i>

22:21.270 --> 22:26.009
<i>as I begin to walk in the morning</i>

22:26.010 --> 22:31.449
<i>In a world where light and dark intersect</i>

22:31.450 --> 22:37.619
<i>catharsis begins to awake</i>

22:37.620 --> 22:42.719
<i>I swore in my shaking heart</i>

22:42.720 --> 22:50.720
<i>that I won't lose anyone anymore...!</i>

22:54.530 --> 22:59.569
<i>Even if my tears flow tomorrow</i>

22:59.570 --> 23:06.279
<i>I'll run through the wind</i>

23:06.280 --> 23:11.319
<i>Release myself towards
the future I selected</i>

23:11.320 --> 23:13.949
<i>to regain it</i>

23:13.950 --> 23:21.050
<i>I won't give up on my wish</i>

23:27.300 --> 23:28.939
It was Akira!

23:28.940 --> 23:32.909
Don't be spouting that crap's
name with that crap voice of yours!

23:32.910 --> 23:34.009
Akira-<i>san</i>?

23:34.010 --> 23:35.939
Shut it, twerp.

23:35.940 --> 23:37.579
If there's a battle...

23:37.580 --> 23:38.910
Mastermind...?

23:38.911 --> 23:39.960
"That Feverish Bond"

23:39.961 --> 23:41.070
That Feverish Bond.
